    "title": "A=1 first-degree double-root radical cube bridge",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact function-field cube identity for retained scalar branches",
    "statement": "Dividing the cancelled scalar ambient identity by the radical of its residual gives W^3=(rad(R_a)^3/R_a)G_L/H in the total quotient ring. Thus the retained core-free cubic double-root and core-one quadratic double-root branches are exact cube problems, and their bounded Picard sections are precisely the canonical cube roots. A closing theorem must use the Hankel/apolar realization to prove the relevant locator ratio is not a cube.",
